Arrays.sort(prims);            // dual-pivot QUICKSORT for primitives

Integer[] objs = {5, 2, 8, 1};
Arrays.sort(objs);             // TIMSORT (stable) for objects

// Stability matters when sorting objects by a key:
record P(String name, int age) {}
P[] people = { new P("Ann", 30), new P("Bob", 30) };
Arrays.sort(people, Comparator.comparingInt(P::age));  // Ann stays before Bob
```
Primitives don't need stability (equal ints are indistinguishable), so quicksort is fine; objects use stable TimSort.

